  :body "Clause 0, X0(e) and the kernel choice. Three of eleven reachable states have two incomparable patterns enabled at once. At theta 0.8, horizon 6: co-application reaches all wants with p 0.26; the list kernel (every linear extension) and interleaving reach them with p 0. At horizon 14 all three give 0.998-1.0. So the semilattice changes the RATE at which wants are reached, not whether they can be. X0(e) as written (flatten; if nothing changes, the semilattice did no work) BREAKS: on a click whose horizon exceeds the cascade's depth, flattening changes nothing whatever the structure. The finding has to be stated relative to the horizon. Interleaving tracks the list kernel, not co-application: the choice that matters is one pattern per step versus several."}
