  :body "software-design/adapter-pattern now produces :impersonation-retired, and its THEN is the discriminator: create a dedicated adapter translating between the EXPECTED interface and the dependency's, and keep that adapter as THE ONLY integration boundary. matrix-ircd fails the second clause \u2014 it is a boundary stacked under IRC's own shape \u2014 so satisfying the pattern retires the impersonation rather than sanctioning it. The guard needs :protocol-declared, and that dependency is the finding: with no declared interface, 'translate to the expected interface' has no referent except whatever the first implementation does. The same pattern, before and after the declaration, produces the impersonation or the seam."}
